  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Adds a generated, externally-accounted FmpzMatrix resource with always-valid zero-filled construction and checked mutation; structural arithmetic and exact FLINT algorithms; aligned formatting; and strict, canonical SJZM v1 serialization/deserialization. The follow-up fixes FLINT-word exponent portability, covers empty and rectangular normal forms plus malformed serialization and failure cleanup under sanitizers, and compares a warmed non-diagonal workload against both legacy FLINT resources and the packed boundary with result equivalence.",
    "risks": [
      "The resource target is intentionally wasm=False until the generated opaque-resource host adapter has a proven WebAssembly lowering.",
      "HNF and SNF expose direct FLINT canonical forms but transformation matrices are deferred to a later multi-result resource protocol.",
      "The current declaration result model has one failure domain per call, so allocation exhaustion and dimension overflow cannot yet be reported separately; FLINT allocation itself may abort rather than return a recoverable status."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Migrate dense ZZ public Matrix storage and operations to FmpzMatrix while retaining the packed implementation as the portable fallback and differential oracle.",
      "Design right-kernel resource semantics together with the public lattice-basis normalization contract instead of freezing an incidental basis at this ABI layer.",
      "Add a typed-Python borrowed traversal witness when the public dense ZZ migration establishes its kernel-facing API."
    ]
  }
